WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:18.189
Henry stared at the flavor board outside the Sweet Shop.

2
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.871
"Mrs. Sweet erased bubble gum banana swirl!"

3
00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:29.748
"She probably decided that if Mr. Tate was going to copy her flavor, she didn't want it anymore," said Maggie.

4
00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:34.384
"Or she's trying to hide all traces of her crime!" chimed in Cole.

5
00:00:34.385 --> 00:00:40.666
"Let's go find Mr. Tate," Henry said.

6
00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:44.488
When they reached the Dessert Den, the electrician's truck was gone.

7
00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:50.305
The front door was standing open as Mr. Tate hurried back and forth carrying boxes inside.

8
00:00:50.306 --> 00:00:56.770
"Good, you're back," he said to the kids. "Grab a box and come on in.

9
00:00:56.771 --> 00:00:59.510
Did you get Mrs. Sweet to confess?"

10
00:00:59.511 --> 00:01:05.035
"We're still working on the case," Henry said. "We have a question.

11
00:01:05.036 --> 00:01:09.227
When did you hang up the menu with your secret flavor on it?"

12
00:01:09.228 --> 00:01:13.537
"Right after Mr. Moss finished painting it on Saturday. Why?"

13
00:01:13.538 --> 00:01:18.119
"Mr. Moss painted your sign?" Cole said, surprised.

14
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.367
Mr. Tate nodded. "At first I thought I'd made a mistake hiring him.

15
00:01:23.368 --> 00:01:28.499
The old guy never stops talking! But he did a fantastic job on the sign."

16
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.736
"Aha!" Henry smiled. "I think I know what happened."

17
00:01:33.737 --> 00:01:36.239
Maggie didn't seem to hear Henry.

18
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.717
"But Mr. Moss is dating Mrs. Sweet!" she blurted out.

19
00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:44.965
"He is?" Mr. Tate frowned. "That proves it!

20
00:01:44.966 --> 00:01:50.481
Mrs. Sweet must have heard about my flavor from him. I knew she was guilty!"

21
00:01:50.482 --> 00:01:54.162
"Mrs. Sweet isn't guilty," Henry said.

22
00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:57.792
"I knew it!" Maggie pointed at Mr. Tate.

23
00:01:57.793 --> 00:02:02.034
"You found out about Mrs. Sweet's new flavor from Mr. Moss!

24
00:02:02.035 --> 00:02:06.018
Then you decided to frame her to drive her out of business!"

25
00:02:06.019 --> 00:02:09.456
"What are you talking about?" Mr. Tate said.

26
00:02:09.457 --> 00:02:15.360
"Wait," Henry said. "Maggie, Mr. Tate isn't guilty either."

27
00:02:15.361 --> 00:02:21.770
"He's not?" Cole said. "Then who is guilty?"

28
00:02:21.771 --> 00:02:29.784
"The guilty person is . . . nobody!" Henry shrugged.

29
00:02:29.785 --> 00:02:34.293
"At least, nobody doing anything wrong on purpose."

30
00:02:34.294 --> 00:02:38.452
"I don't get it." Maggie was still glaring at Mr. Tate.

31
00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:40.946
But she looked a little less certain.

32
00:02:40.947 --> 00:02:46.854
"Everybody in Belltown knows Mr. Moss likes to gossip," Henry began.

33
00:02:46.855 --> 00:02:52.254
"I only moved here a month ago, and I already know that," Mr. Tate agreed.

34
00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:56.776
"Usually Mr. Moss' gossip is harmless," Henry said.

35
00:02:56.777 --> 00:03:00.024
"He just likes to share interesting news.

36
00:03:00.025 --> 00:03:06.136
I bet he thought your special flavor was interesting, so he mentioned it to Mrs. Sweet."

37
00:03:06.137 --> 00:03:12.302
"Right," Mr. Tate said. "And she decided to steal it to ruin my grand opening!"

38
00:03:12.303 --> 00:03:15.012
"Not exactly," Henry said.

39
00:03:15.013 --> 00:03:18.922
"My guess is that he didn't tell her where he'd seen it."

40
00:03:18.923 --> 00:03:21.530
"I get it now!" Maggie said.

41
00:03:21.531 --> 00:03:26.938
"Mrs. Sweet thought the flavor sounded interesting, so she added it to her menu."

42
00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:33.475
Cole nodded. "Without realizing that she was stealing Mr. Tate's flavor!"

43
00:03:33.476 --> 00:03:36.738
He frowned. "But wait.

44
00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:44.111
If this is just a misunderstanding, why did Mrs. Sweet behave so suspiciously when we talked to her earlier?"

45
00:03:44.112 --> 00:03:49.156
"Because she didn't want to get her boyfriend in trouble," Henry said.

46
00:03:49.157 --> 00:03:53.346
"That's right," a voice said from the door.

47
00:03:53.347 --> 00:03:59.449
"Mrs. Sweet!" Maggie cried. "What are you doing here?"

48
00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:05.812
"I came to apologize to Mr. Tate." Mrs. Sweet stepped toward Mr. Tate.

49
00:04:05.813 --> 00:04:09.672
"I'm sorry for accidentally stealing your flavor.

50
00:04:09.673 --> 00:04:14.305
It took me a little while to find Mr. Moss and confirm what happened.

51
00:04:14.306 --> 00:04:17.090
He's sorry too, of course.

52
00:04:17.091 --> 00:04:22.657
He didn't realize that flavor was supposed to be a secret until I told him a few minutes ago.

53
00:04:22.658 --> 00:04:25.997
I took the flavor off our menu right away."

54
00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.468
"Oh, I see." Mr. Tate looked sheepish.

55
00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:34.332
"Thank you for the explanation, Mrs. Sweet. Maybe I owe you an apology too.

56
00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:37.054
I was ready to believe the worst about you."

57
00:04:37.055 --> 00:04:43.157
"It's all right." Mrs. Sweet smiled. "By the way, welcome to Belltown.

58
00:04:43.158 --> 00:04:45.632
I hope we can be friends."

59
00:04:45.633 --> 00:04:49.515
"How can you say that?" Maggie blurted out in surprise.

60
00:04:49.516 --> 00:04:52.578
"The Dessert Den is your competition!"

61
00:04:52.579 --> 00:04:59.232
Mrs. Sweet chuckled. "Perhaps. But everyone loves ice cream.

62
00:04:59.233 --> 00:05:02.435
I'm sure there's room for both businesses."

63
00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:05.614
"Of course, we'll be friends," Mr. Tate said.

64
00:05:05.615 --> 00:05:08.245
"And I hope you'll stop by my grand opening tomorrow.

65
00:05:08.246 --> 00:05:12.591
All of you," he added, looking at the Lemonade Detectives.

66
00:05:12.592 --> 00:05:17.330
"That reminds me—I owe you kids your five-dollar detective fee."

67
00:05:17.331 --> 00:05:22.025
He reached into his pocket for the money.

68
00:05:22.026 --> 00:05:24.796
"Here's another five dollars from me."

69
00:05:24.797 --> 00:05:30.597
Mrs. Sweet took a bill out of her purse and handed it to Henry.

70
00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:36.894
"For clearing my name and for believing in me despite the evidence."

71
00:05:36.895 --> 00:05:41.058
"It was only circumstantial evidence," Maggie said.

72
00:05:41.059 --> 00:05:50.381
Mrs. Sweet laughed. "In any case, you three are welcome to all the free ice cream you can eat for the rest of the summer."

73
00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:53.327
"Good idea," Mr. Tate chimed in.

74
00:05:53.328 --> 00:05:57.663
"You kids are welcome to free dessert here for the rest of the summer as well."

75
00:05:57.664 --> 00:06:09.248
"Wow, thanks! That's what I call a sweet reward!" Cole licked his lips.
